{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And I will harden.</b> Since the El desires the repentance of the wicked and not their death, as it says: חַי אָנִי נְאֻם ה', אִם אֶחְפֹּץ בְּמוֹת הָרָשָׁע, כִּי אִם בְּשׁוּב הָרָשָׁע מִדַּרְכּוֹ וְחָיָה (Ezekiel 33:11), He said that He would multiply His signs and wonders — this, in order to bring the Egyptians back in repentance, by making known to them His greatness and His lovingkindness through the signs and wonders, as it says: בַּעֲבוּר זֹאת הֶעֱמַדְתִּיךָ, בַּעֲבוּר הַרְאוֹתְךָ אֶת כֹּחִי (Exodus 9:16). Together with this, the intent was that Israel would see and fear, as it says: לְמַעַן שִׁיתִי אֹתֹתַי אֵלֶּה בְּקִרְבּוֹ, וּלְמַעַן תְּסַפֵּר (Exodus 10:1–2). And there is no doubt that were it not for the hardness of heart, Pharaoh would have sent Israel away without doubt — not by way of repentance and submission to the blessed El, relenting from being a rebel, even though he recognized His greatness and goodness, but rather because he was unable to endure the affliction of the plagues any longer, as his servants stated in saying: הֲטֶרֶם תֵּדַע כִּי אָבְדָה מִצְרָיִם (Exodus 10:7) — and this would not have been repentance at all. But if Pharaoh had been willing to submit to the blessed El and return to Him in complete repentance, nothing would have prevented him. Now the blessed El said, 'And I will harden Pharaoh's heart' — that he would steel himself to endure the plagues and not send Israel away out of fear of the plagues — 'לְמַעַן שִׁיתִי אֹתֹתַי אֵלֶּה בְּקִרְבּוֹ,' so that through them they would recognize My greatness and My goodness and the Egyptians would return in true repentance; 'וּלְמַעַן תְּסַפֵּר' — you, Israel, who witness their affliction — 'בְּאָזְנֵי בִנְךָ,' to make known that the El does all these things to a man in order to bring him back to Himself, and this when they search their deeds at the onset of some affliction upon them."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:24:47.496186011Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}